A||||2||My7Fieros||Ogre/Transmission guys.....I need some help||||5||
Z||000000||My7Fieros||08-29-2000||12:45 AM||||Ok, in addition to the Formula Im restoring, Im also working on an 87 GT. The car is in extra great shape, blah blah blah. However, Ive noticed that at right around 1400 RPM, it does this up/down/up/down shift thing. Hard to describe, but its almost like it shifts up alittle to early. It gets kinda jerky, and lacks power at that RPM range. This is under normal steady acceleration from stop conditions. If you just "punch" it off the line, no prob....but for normal driving, it almost seems to get confused at 1400......any ideas? tia, Brian||||reg||5
Z||000001||mrfiero||08-29-2000||01:50 AM||||It sounds like this GT is an auto.  It could be the TCC (torque convertor lock-up switch).  There is a 4 prong plug on the side of the tranny.....unplug this then drive it.  If this up-down thing has vanished then you know it's the switch.<P>They are relatively cheap, but sort of a pain to replace.  You have to remove the side pan on the tranny.<BR>   ||||reg||6
Z||000002||theogre||08-29-2000||11:52 AM||||At 1400 he's likely going to slow for TC lock. That and the tranny only locks in third gear and at a constant speed over 35.<P>It sounds like there's an engine problem more than the tranny. I'd check things like timing MAP and TPS. Those can all cause engine performance holes. A performance hole could cause a shift problem if it's doing it near a shift point.<P>If it is the tranny I'd start with checking fluid level and condition. Those will both cause nasty shifts. Does it do this at the 1-2 shift or the 2-3 shift or both? It could be a real problem in the tranny or just some dirt in there. Some people claim good luck with putting some cleaner in it. If the cleaner fixes it I'd do a fluid and filter on it soon. It could also be that the TV cable is a hair out of whack. That will also throw off shifting.<P>There's now an article on TH125 in my cave that may help. follow the link at the bottom of the page. I'll be adding more to that article in future. (For example the fact that the TV adjust latch is on the tranny end of the cable on some versions is not in the haynes book. The procedure is still valid but if you didn't realize the latch moved.....)<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 08-29-2000).]||||reg||1
